WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:04.600
Where I come from

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.609
it seems like everybody has an immigrant story.

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:09.470
The harbor in Buenos Aires

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.459
beckoned newcomers from over the world.

00:00:12.459 --> 00:00:17.199
My ancestors were Italian, Spanish and Indian.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:19.949
And the only thing I had to do was go out
of the house

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:23.779
to experience a different language a different
culture.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:25.609
I remember sneaking out in spring

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:28.789
to celebrate Passover with my Jewish friends

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:30.730
we also had Lebanese neighbors

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.599
and their religious festivities

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.620
also became part of our celebrations in the
family.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.640
I think that all Argentines carry a piece
of the world with them

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.670
and that’s why it’s relatively easy for
me

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:45.039
to walk in other people’s shoes.

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:49.470
My work is not only about political and social
issues.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.969
I want to find out, what’s below the surface

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:56.390
the issues and the stories that have shaped
the people.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.390
I want to show

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.530
that even though we are all different,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.159
there is a general human condition

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:03.300
that connects us all.

